# BC250 category: experimental
# Ollama model: exp-qwen38-4b-empero-q6-k
# Source: empero-ai/Qwen3.8-4B-Distill-GGUF @ latest
# GGUF: Qwen3.8-4B-Q6_K.gguf
# License: Apache-2.0
#
# Intended role:
# - Compact reasoning/general assistant experiment
# - Compare against task models and larger Qwen3.5/Qwen3.8 candidates
# - Test whether a ~3.56 GB Q6_K model offers a useful latency/quality point
#
# The upstream model is a reasoning model and emits a <think> block by default.

FROM /var/lib/bc250-llm-server/gguf/experiments/exp-qwen38-4b-empero-q6-k/Qwen3.8-4B-Q6_K.gguf

# BC-250: force full GPU offload.
PARAMETER num_gpu 99

# Preserve the SYSTEM prefix when old context is evicted.
PARAMETER num_keep 256

# Small enough to test a useful 32K window while retaining substantial UMA headroom.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# Upstream recommended sampling for Qwen3.8-4B.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0

SYSTEM """You are an experimental multilingual reasoning assistant for German-, French-, and English-speaking users.
Solve the requested task accurately and completely. Use reasoning when it materially improves the answer, but keep the final answer direct and useful.
Preserve important names, numbers, dates, terminology, and qualifications. Distinguish source facts from inference and state uncertainty instead of fabricating details.
Respond in the language requested by the user, or the language of the latest request when unspecified."""
